    "result": "Perfect! All tests are passing. Here's a summary of the fixes I made:\n\n## Fixed Issues\n\n**1. Governance module exports** (`src/finetune/index.js`):\n   - Added named exports for `APPROVAL_STATUSES`, `DATA_SENSITIVITY_LEVELS`, `GOVERNANCE_SECTIONS`, and `RISK_LEVELS`\n   - The test was trying to import these as named imports, but they were only available in the default export\n   - Kept the default export intact for backwards compatibility\n\n**2. Toxicity metric signature** (`src/eval/metrics.js`):\n   - Changed `toxicityMetric(outputs, bannedTerms)` to `toxicityMetric(outputs, references, bannedTerms)`\n   - The function is called by `runEvaluations` with `(outputs, references)` for all metrics\n   - Previously, `references` was being treated as the `bannedTerms` parameter, causing incorrect scoring\n   - Now `references` is accepted but unused (which is correct), and `bannedTerms` defaults to the default list\n\nAll 28 tests now pass across 8 test files. The changes maintain full backwards compatibility with all existing public exports.",
